ymptoms the farmer describes, and recommend an in-person inspection to confirm.\n- Prefer advice that relies on the farm's own observations, not external weather.\n- Reply in the farmer's language: Kannada if they wrote Kannada, else English.\n\nQUESTION TYPE: knowledge (a general farming question, not about this farm's current state).\n- Answer it from AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE. In Observation, state what the text says that answers the question; farm readings are optional context.\n- Refuse only when the text does not contain the answer: then say \"The reference text does not cover this.\" and name exactly what is missing. Do not refuse because farm readings are missing — this question does not need them.\n\n# FOCUS FOR THIS QUESTION (pest)\nAsk about or interpret described signs of pest pressure (borer holes, chewed leaves, discoloration). Advise scouting and integrated pest management; chemical control only if justified.\n\n# FARM\nName: Demo Farm\nCrop: sugarcane\nLocation: Mandya\nFarmer: Demo Farmer\nToday: 05 October 2026\n\n# CURRENT OBSERVATION\n- Time: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC (node demo-node-1)\n- Sensor values: as in SENSOR READINGS below\n- GPS: 12.806987279716143, 74.93193321230041\n\n# SENSOR READINGS (latest)\n- Taken: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC\n- Temperature: 27.9 C\n- Humidity: 72.4 %\n- Soil moisture: 32.3 %\n\n# RECENT HISTORY\nOnly one observation on record — no comparison possible yet.\nObservations on record: 10 (most recent first).\n\n# ACTIVE ALERTS\nAddress these FIRST:\n- [critical] Node offline (no contact for 50275 min)\n\n# AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information:\n- One-day Farmer Training Programme on \"Identification and Management of Major Sugarcane Borers\" under SC-SP Plan, at ICAR-IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar (Maharashtra).\n  - One-day Farmer Training Programme on \"Integrated Management of White Grubs Infesting Sugarcane,\" at the same Biological Control Centre.\n  - Training program on \"Biological Control of Pests in Sugarcane,\" organized by the ICAR-IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar.\n  - Launch of \"Parthenium Awareness Week\" (16–22 August 2024) by ICAR-IISR — a weed-management/invasive-species public awareness initiative.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Key Facts:\n- Sugarcane seed (spring planting) online applications opened 1 February 2025 — confirms an active, current-season seed distribution channel.\n- 2024 dated activities: Parthenium Awareness Week (16–22 August 2024), sugarcane borer identification training, white grub management training, Agriculture Leadership Award 2024.\n- Farmer helpline channel: SMS/photo submission via mobile phone or email to the IISR Nodal Officer.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information:\n- National Seminar on \"Mechanization of Sugarcane Cultivation,\" and a five-day residential training programme titled \"Importance of Mechanization in Sugarcane-Based Cropping Systems\" (Hindi: गन्ना आधारित फसल प्रणाली में यांत्रिकीकरण का महत्व) — both reinforcing mechanization as a current institutional priority, consistent with the machinery documents already in this knowledge base.\n  - ICAR-IISR, Lucknow was conferred the Agriculture Leadership Award 2024.\n- These activities collectively confirm that, as of the 2024–2025 period, biological pest control (borers, white grubs), weed awareness (Parthenium), and mechanization remain IISR's active extension priorities — directly reinforcing (rather than contradicting) the pest management and machinery guidance already sourced from the institute's 2017 bulletin.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Important Recommendations:\n- Farmers or advisory-system builders seeking real-time, query-specific sugarcane troubleshooting (as opposed to general package-of-practices guidance) should be directed to IISR's SMS/photo-based farmer helpline rather than relying solely on static documents, since this channel provides current, personalized diagnosis.\n- Given IISR's active 2024 focus on biological control training for borers and white grubs, any advisory content on these two pests (see the Pest Management document) should be treated as current best practice, not superseded guidance — the institute's own 2024 programming reinforces rather than revises the 2017 bulletin's biological-control recommendations for these specific pests.\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - ಸಮಯ: 2026‑07‑26 16:40 UTC (node demo‑node‑1) - ತಾಪಮಾನ: 23.0 °C (ಬದಲಾವಣೆಯಾಗಿಲ್ಲ) - ಆರ್ದ್ರತೆ: 64.2 % (ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಇಳಿದಿದೆ) - ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶ: 0.0 % (ವಾಲ್ಯೂಮೆಟ್ರಿಕ್) – ಹಿಂದಿನ ಮಾಪನದಿಂದ 49 % ಕುಸಿತ (49 % → 0 %) - ಸಕ್ರಿಯ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ: ...\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - ಸಮಯ: 2026‑07‑26 16:40 UTC (node demo‑node‑1) - ತಾಪಮಾನ: 23.0 °C (ಬದಲಾವಣೆ ಇಲ್ಲ) - ಆರ್ದ್ರತೆ: 64.2 % (ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಇಳಿದಿದೆ) - ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶ: 0.0 % (ವಾಲ್ಯೂಮೆಟ್ರಿಕ್) – ಹಿಂದಿನ ಮಾಪನದಿಂದ 49 % ಕುಸಿತ (49 % → 0 %) - ಸಕ್ರಿಯ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ: **Low ...\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - Vision: ಚಿತ್ರವನ್ನು ಬ್ರೌನ್ ಸ್ಪಾಟ್ (brown spot) ಎಂದು 95% ವಿಶ್ವಾಸದೊಂದಿಗೆ ವರ್ಗೀಕರಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ. - Temperature: 25.0 °C - Humidity: 55.0 % - Soil moisture: 40.0 % - Active alerts: - [warning] High humidity 88 % (ರೋಗದ ಅಪಾಯ) - ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nNodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "farmer": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi."}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "sarvam": "Sir, please confirm the date of conducting the Sugarcane Borer Training by IIRSAR.", "groq": "When did IISR conduct sugarcane borer training? confirm dates."}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8314, "sarvam