owledge).  \n\n**Recommendations**  \n\n- **Immediate actions**  \n  1. Contact your nearest Karnataka KVK (e.g., KVK Mandya) or a certified seed supplier and ask for the list of varieties that are registered for the tropical zone of Karnataka and are noted as resistant to red rot, smut and wilt.  \n  2. Procure only disease‑free, nursery‑derived (or tissue‑culture) setts of the selected variety.  \n  3. Plan planting at the recommended seed rate of **25,000–30,000 setts / ha** with **≈ 90 cm row spacing**.  \n\n- **Monitoring advice**  \n  1. Before planting, inspect the setts for any signs of rot, discoloration or pest damage.  \n  2. After planting, monitor emergence and early growth; ensure that at least 40–45 % of buds germinate, which indicates good seed health.  \n  3. Keep an eye on the field for early symptoms of red rot, smut or wilt, especially in the first 2–3 months.  \n\n- **When to seek expert help**  \n  1. If you are unable to obtain a clear list of disease‑resistant varieties from the KVK or seed supplier.  \n  2. If the setts you receive show any disease symptoms or poor germination despite following the recommended seed rate and spacing.  \n  3. If disease symptoms (e.g., wilting, red lesions, smut sori) appear in the crop, request an in‑person inspection by a crop‑protective specialist.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 2.14, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 217, "completion_tokens": 71, "seconds": 0.61, "status": "ok", "seq": 16}, {"purpose": "answer", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "prompt_tokens": 1976, "completion_tokens": 1036, "seconds": 2.86, "status": "ok", "seq": 17}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 1428, "completion_tokens": 954, "seconds": 2.14, "status": "ok", "seq": 18}]}
