at relies on the farm's own observations, not external weather.\n- Reply in the farmer's language: Kannada if they wrote Kannada, else English.\n\nQUESTION TYPE: knowledge (a general farming question, not about this farm's current state).\n- Answer it from AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE. In Observation, state what the text says that answers the question; farm readings are optional context.\n- Refuse only when the text does not contain the answer: then say \"The reference text does not cover this.\" and name exactly what is missing. Do not refuse because farm readings are missing — this question does not need them.\n\n# FOCUS FOR THIS QUESTION (irrigation)\nJudge irrigation timing from the soil-moisture level and its trend and the crop stage. Say whether to irrigate now, wait, or hold, and why.\n\n# FARM\nName: Demo Farm\nCrop: sugarcane\nLocation: Mandya\nFarmer: Demo Farmer\nToday: 05 October 2026\n\n# CURRENT OBSERVATION\n- Time: 2026-10-05 06:07 UTC (node demo-node-1)\n- Sensor values: as in SENSOR READINGS below\n- GPS: n/a, n/a\n\n# SENSOR READINGS (latest)\n- Taken: 2026-10-05 06:07 UTC\n- Temperature: 27.5 C\n- Humidity: 70.0 %\n- Soil moisture: 42.0 %\n\n# RECENT HISTORY\nTrends (compare current vs earlier observation):\n- Soil moisture unchanged by 0.0% compared to the previous observation (42.0% -> 42.0%).\n- Humidity unchanged by 0.0% compared to the previous observation (70.0% -> 70.0%).\n- Temperature unchanged by 0.0C compared to the previous observation (27.5C -> 27.5C).\nObservations on record: 10 (most recent first).\n\n# ACTIVE ALERTS\nNo active alerts.\n\n# SENSOR PATTERN CHECK (FlyBrain)\nThe latest sensor reading scored 0.23 on the FlyBrain pattern check, within this farm's normal range (threshold 0.25; synthetic test graph (not the real fly connectome)).\n\n# AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE\nGovernment Schemes for Farmers: Karnataka Department of Agriculture and Central Schemes — Main Information:\n### National Food Security Mission (NFSM)\nCovers Rice, Pulses, and Commercial Crops including **Cotton and Sugarcane**, plus Coarse Cereals/Nutri-Cereals sub-missions. Provides for 100-hectare area cluster demonstrations of improved production technologies and cropping systems, distribution of improved-variety seeds, inputs for Integrated Nutrient and Pest Management, agricultural machinery, pump sets, and drip irrigation sets under subsidy, along with farmer training. Incentives are directly transferred to farmers' bank accounts (DBT) to promote adoption of improved technologies.\n\n### Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) — Micro Irrigation\nA centrally sponsored scheme facilitating installation of micro-irrigation units (sprinkler and drip) for all categories of farmers, especially small and marginal farmers, at **90% subsidy**, to increase water-use efficiency.\n\nSugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information:\n- **Karnataka-specific data**: 32 irrigations required per season; average yield 85.5 t/ha; irrigation water required to produce 1.0 kg of sugar is 266 kg — among the highest of all sugarcane states reported, reflecting Karnataka's tropical multi-irrigation cropping pattern.\n- **Net irrigation water requirement by technique (Karnataka, mm/year)**: furrow irrigation 1,878 mm; skip furrow 1,408 mm; sprinkler 1,325 mm; drip 1,186 mm — showing drip irrigation can reduce net water requirement by roughly 37% compared to conventional furrow irrigation for the same crop water demand.\n\n### Water-economizing methods\n1. **Skip-furrow/alternate furrow irrigation**: one row is skipped and irrigation applied only to alternate furrows, saving 30–40% water without reducing cane productivity.\n\nIntegrated Insect-Pest Management in Sugarcane — Main Information:\n- **Early shoot and root borer**: Application of Chlorpyriphos 20 EC at 5 litres/ha in 1,600–1,800 litres water (3 ml/litre) on cane setts in furrows at planting. Collection and destruction of infested shoots on a campaign basis from March to May is also recommended.\n- **Termite**: Chlorpyriphos 20 EC at 5 litres/ha in 1,600–1,800 litres water applied over setts in furrows at planting.\n- **Whitefly**: Removal of lower leaves followed by foliar application of imidacloprid (0.005%) + 2% urea; urea solution should be prepared first, then imidacloprid added, to avoid coagulation.\n- **Mealy bug**: Sett treatment with imidacloprid 70 WG/SP or thiamethoxam 70 WG/SP (25 g a.i./ha), followed by foliar spraying of imidacloprid 17.8 SL (0.05%) at cane formation stage.\n- **Rodents**: Zinc phosphide (2%) baiting followed by bromadiolone baiting.\n\nSugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information:\n- General guidance: irrigation water depth of 7–8 cm per application is recommended, with frequency varying by crop phase — approximately once every 7 days during germination (1–35 days after planting, DAP), once every 10 days during tillering (36–100 DAP), once every 7 days during grand growth (101–270 DAP), and once every 15 days during maturity (271 DAP to harvest), adjusted for rainfall.\n- Subtropical regions typically need 6–8 irrigations across the season; tropical regions (including Karnataka) may need 20–36 irrigations due to climatic conditions, annual rainfall, planting season, crop duration, and soil type.\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: Is my soil too dry right now?\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"15 cm\" (this number is not in Gage's sources); \"10–15 mm\" (this number is not in Gage's sources); \"3–5 days\" (this number is not in Gage's sources); +6. **Observation** - Active alert: **[critical] Node ...\nFarmer: Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation:** Agricultural knowledge states that the recommended irrigation depth per application for sugarcane is **7–8 cm**. **Analysis:** Therefore, each irrigation event should deliver water to a depth of 7–8 cm to meet the crop’s ...\nFarmer: Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"After irrigation, the soil‑moisture sensor should show an increase from the pre‑irrigation level\" (not in Gage's sources); \"The crop should show signs of water stress (wilting, yellowing) if ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nPrathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.", "farmer": "Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku."}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.", "sarvam": "For each irrigation, the amount of water supplied is measured in centimeters.Me, water should be added."}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8499, "sarvam": 0.8402}, "retrieved": [{"source": "government_schemes/01_karnataka_and_central_govt_schemes_for_farmers.md", "section": "Government Schemes for Farmers: Karnataka Department of Agriculture and Central Schemes — Main Information", "score": 0.8499, "via": "original"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.8455, "via": "original"}, {"source": "pests/01_insect_pest_management.md", "section": "Integrated Insect-Pest Management in Sugarcane — Main Information", "score": 0.8402, "via": "original"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.8402, "via": "sarvam"}], "raw_answer": "**Observation:**  \nಕೃಷಿ ಜ್ಞಾನದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಕ್ಕರೆಕಬ್ಬು ಪ್ರತಿ ನೀರಾವರಿ ಅನ್ವಯದಲ್ಲಿ 7 – 8 ಸೆಂ.ಮೀ. ನೀರಿನ ಆಳವನ್ನು ನೀಡುವಂತೆ ಶಿಫಾರಸು ಮಾಡಲಾಗಿದೆ.\n\n**Analysis:**  \nಆದ್ದರಿಂದ, ಪ್ರತಿ ನೀರಾವರಿ ವೇಳೆ 7 – 8 ಸೆಂ.ಮೀ. ನೀರನ್ನು ಮಣ್ಣಿಗೆ ತಲುಪುವಂತೆ ಹಂಚಬೇಕು; ಇದರಿಂದ ಬೆಳೆ ಬೆಳವಣಿಗೆಯ ವಿವಿಧ ಹಂತಗಳಿಗೆ ಅಗತ್ಯವಾದ ನೀರಿನ ಪ್ರಮಾಣ ಪೂರೈಸಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ.\n\n**Confidence:**  \nHigh – ನೇರವಾಗಿ ಕೃಷಿ ಜ್ಞಾನದಲ್ಲಿ ನೀಡಲಾಗಿದೆ.\n\n**Recommendations:**  \n\n- **Immediate actions:**  \n  - ಪ್ರತಿ ನೀರಾವರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ 7 – 8 ಸೆಂ.ಮೀ. ನೀರಿನ ಆಳವನ್ನು ಸಾಧಿಸಲು ನೀರಿನ ಹರಿವು ಮತ್ತು ಸಮಯವನ್ನು ಸಮರ್ಪಕವಾಗಿ ನಿಯಂತ್ರಿಸಿ.\n\n- **Monitoring advice:**  \n  - ನೀರಾವರಿಯ ನಂತರ ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶ ಸೆನ್ಸರ್ ಮೌಲ್ಯ ಹೆಚ್ಚಿದೆಯೇ ಎಂದು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ.  \n  - ಕಬ್ಬು ಎಲೆಗಳು ಮಡಚಿಕೊಳ್ಳುವ, ಹಳದಿ ಬಣ್ಣದ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳು ಕಾಣಿಸದಿರುವುದನ್ನು ಗಮನಿಸಿ.\n\n- **When to seek expert help:**  \n  - ನೀರಾವರಿಯ ನಂತರ ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶದಲ್ಲಿ ಏರಿಕೆ ಕಾಣದಿದ್ದರೆ ಅಥವಾ ಕಬ್ಬು ನೀರಿನ ಕೊರತೆಯ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳು (ವಿಲುಪ್ತತೆ, ಹಳದಿ ಎಲೆಗಳು) ತೋರಿದರೆ, ಸ್ಥಳೀಯ ಕೃಷಿ ಅಧಿಕಾರಿ ಅಥವಾ ತಾಂತ್ರಿಕರನ್ನು ಸಂಪರ್ಕಿಸಿ.", "claims": ["supported: Irrigation water depth of 7–8 cm per application is recommended for sugarcane", "supported: Each irrigation should deliver 7–8 cm of water depth to the soil", "unsupported: Providing 7–8 cm per irrigation supplies the water needed for all growth stages", "supported: Immediate action is to control flow and timing to achieve 7–8 cm depth per irrigation", "unsupported: After irrigation, check if soil moisture sensor value has increased", "unsupported: Observe for leaf curling and yellowing as signs of water stress", "unsupported: Seek local agricultural officer if soil moisture does not rise or if water‑stress symptoms appear"], "unsupported": ["unsupported: Providing 7–8 cm per irrigation supplies the water needed for all growth stages", "unsupported: After irrigation, check if soil moisture sensor value has increased", "unsupported: Observe for leaf curling and yellowing as signs of water stress", "unsupported: Seek local agricultural officer if soil moisture does not rise or if water‑stress symptoms appear"], "final_answer": "Please double-check before acting: \"Providing 7–8 cm per irrigation supplies the water needed for all growth stages\" (not in Gage's sources); \"After irrigation, check if soil moisture sensor value has increased\" (not in Gage's sources); \"Observe for leaf curling and yellowing as signs of water stress\" (not in Gage's sources); +1.\n\n**Observation:**  \nಕೃಷಿ ಜ್ಞಾನದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಕ್ಕರೆಕಬ್ಬು ಪ್ರತಿ ನೀರಾವರಿ ಅನ್ವಯದಲ್ಲಿ 7 – 8 ಸೆಂ.ಮೀ. ನೀರಿನ ಆಳವನ್ನು ನೀಡುವಂತೆ ಶಿಫಾರಸು ಮಾಡಲಾಗಿದೆ.\n\n**Analysis:**  \nಆದ್ದರಿಂದ, ಪ್ರತಿ ನೀರಾವರಿ ವೇಳೆ 7 – 8 ಸೆಂ.ಮೀ. ನೀರನ್ನು ಮಣ್ಣಿಗೆ